,"id":"e04396a0da945e3723f2bac74d32ee0d","originalFileName":"031488d3-a59f-40bd-af7c-479d262ca9dc-attachment.json","ext":".json","contentType":"application/json","contentLength":4919,"name":"newspec-c/evidence/hallu/hallu-nh/evidence/hallu/HL-N5-B.json"},"type":"attachment"},{"link":{"id":"b578b3c61787fa282a12daaf7baa98f1","originalFileName":"9b9bdd1a-d544-4223-a49c-36e33c8cd60a-attachment.json","ext":".json","name":"newspec-c/evidence/hallu/hallu-nh/grading/TC-14-S46-HL-N5-B.judge.json","contentType":"application/json","used":true,"missed":false,"contentLength":63307},"type":"attachment"},{"link":{"used":true,"missed":false,"id":"6474455a6fa0f4dbaa72edee95e61fa0","originalFileName":"02be1627-83e4-4e85-987d-266a6d86e186-attachment.json","ext":".json","contentType":"application/json","contentLength":6023,"name":"lane result (newspec-c/results.json)"},"type":"attachment"}],"error":{"message":"newspec-c: failed → failed (failed (the lane flagged no product issue))\nDev <dev address> (main 8b4be94a), live models (every call Haiku 4.5 us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0, no fallback; generateNote providerMs 7.1–15.1 s, parsePreRoundNotes 4.5–5.3 s), under runs/.dev.lock, browsers in UTC; datasets hallu-hosp + hallu-nh (new specs hallu-hosp/-nh.spec.ts + hallu-lib.ts), 10 synthetic fixtures (5 Hospital, 5 Nursing Home) × arm A (pre-round Save Note → summary → Encounter → Generate) and arm B (same words in the Encounter only → Generate); only prefixed rows created, all deleted (0 remaining, 0 changes to other rows). Trap verdicts by the fixture regexes, 13 'unclear'/false hits settled by the agent's reading (review.agent.json, a person confirms). Preston-kit judge (grade.mjs, claude-opus-5-5 ×2) on all 20 notes: 20/20 uncalibrated FAIL (U1 on every note, U2 on 16), beside, needs a person. Arm A (real flow) 4/10 pass (HL-H1, HL-H4, HL-N2, HL-N5); needs 9/10. Failing: HL-H2 (CAP, ICU), HL-H3 (nephrology), HL-H5 (asthma, obesity), HL-N1 (hypothyroidism), HL-N3 (hypertension), HL-N4 (BPH). Arm B (no summary) 6/10 (fails HL-H2, HL-N1, HL-N3, HL-N5). Hospital A 2/5, NH A 2/5. Every failing note quoted in summary.json; a person confirms each FAIL (Preston's kit, uncalibrated)."},"testCase":{"id":"132eda6c63ec0ecb1864701837ea30ab","externalId":"fe67ef436f4d33dd396dfaa6e927e6b8","name":"[dev] S46 TFA-95204 AC 3 / UAT 3.2: 5 Hospital + 5 Nursing Home hallucination-trap fixtures, a fixture passes only if no trap is invented in its note (9/10)","fullName":"TC-14 In-Room Dictation & Note Generation › TC-14/S46"},"descriptionHtml":"<p><b>Case priority: P0 · stated in the UAT / ticket AC</b> · UAT 3.4; TFA-92592 AC 5; TFA-95204 AC 2 · “No diagnosis, medication decision, or action appears in the note unless it was dictated or typed”.</p><div class=\"roundai-bug\"><p><b>Bug N15 · S0 · new</b></p><p>The AI note adds content that was not dictated: diagnoses ('consistent with pneumonia', 'prerenal azotemia'), recommendations, and in discharge summaries 'Stable per physician assessment' / 'tolerated treatment and improved'</p><p>Tickets: <span translate=\"no\">TFA-92592 AC 5 (TFA-95204 development backlog)</span> · counts as a QA bug: yes · found on: dev + local (43c38a4f)</p><p>Note: Dev, live Haiku: TC-14/S19 9/11, TC-14/S11 pool 9/10 (H-04), and the TC-18/S07 discharge notes. P0 by the rubric for invented clinical content; the note owner to confirm. AI-judged content; merged without a person's check (Quinn 2026-10-20). TFA-95204 traps 2026-10-20 (dev, 10 fixtures): real flow 4/10 clean, without the pre-round summary 6/10. Medication / number → diagnosis start in the summary's background bullets (albuterol → asthma, BMI 31 → obesity, levothyroxine → hypothyroidism, tamsulosin → BPH) and the note copies them; hedges, 'BP 124 → hypertension' and 'call the ICU → escalate to ICU' are invented by the note model itself (also without the summary). The course refresh writes the note's inventions back into the stored background (next day starts from them). Negations kept 4/4. docs/2026-10-20-tfa95204-cases.zh.md, docs/2026-10-20-tfa95204-pipeline-diff.zh.md.</p><p>Other cases of the same bug (counted once): <span translate=\"no\">TC-14/S19, TC-14/S40, TC-14/S41, TC-14/S42, TC-14/S43</span></p></div><div class=\"rc-approach\"><p><b>Approach</b> · TC-14 In-Room Dictation &amp; Note Generation · <b>S46</b> TFA-95204 AC 3 / UAT 3.2: 5 Hospital + 5 Nursing Home hallucination-trap fixtures, a fixture passes only if no trap is invented in its note (9/10)</p><p><b>UAT steps / ticket ACs covered:</b></p><ul><li><b>U5</b> The note reflects only what was dictated or stored, and undictated sections read 'Not dictated'. No supplied diagnosis, invented exam finding or normal, guessed unit on an ambiguous value, 'No past m … (UAT TC-14; UAT 3.4; TFA-92592 AC 5; TFA-94229 R8) — gate: blocked: TFA-92592 ready for pr; TFA-94229 in progress</li><li><b>U18</b> No diagnosis, medication decision or action appears in the note unless it was dictated or typed (&quot;the app documents, the physician decides&quot;): a drug never implies its indication, a value never become … (TFA-95204 AC 2; TFA-95204 AC 3; UAT 3.4; TFA-92592 AC 5)</li><li><b>T4</b> No dictated fact silently disappears from the note (Principle 2). (TFA-94229 R9) — gate: blocked: TFA-94229 in progress</li><li><b>U14</b> Steps 1 to 4 are repeated in Nursing Home, and every expected result holds in both Hospital and Nursing Home. (UAT TC-14 step 5; UAT 3.3; TFA-92592 AC 14) — gate: blocked: TFA-92592 ready for pr</li></ul><p><b>Test design technique: </b>Decision table (decision-table) — List the combinations of several conditions and check each one, to see that the result follows the rule.</p><p><b>Given </b>HL-H1–HL-H5 (Hospital: SOAP ×4, H&amp;P ×1) and HL-N1–HL-N5 (Nursing Home: SNF follow-up ×4, SNF admission ×1), 30 traps over the five families</p><p><b>When </b>Arm A (real flow) per fixture; arm B recorded beside</p><p><b>Then </b>At least 9 of 10 arm-A notes invent none of their traps; every failing note quoted</p><p><b>Pass rule (oracle, excerpt): </b>Fixture pass = no trap 'invented' in the A note (unclear hits count only after a person settles them). 3.2: pass at 9/10. The kit grade (U1/U2/U5/U7/N2 …) is reported beside, uncalibrated</p><p><b>Where it ran: </b>newspec-c (new Playwright specs) on dev; test method AICHECK · AI output check; lane planned in the matrix: AI check (automated)</p><p><small>S46 is our own case number (its number in the coverage matrix cases/TC-14.matrix.json), not a step number of the UAT document.</small></p></div><div class=\"rc-triage\"><p><b>Triage (2026-10-14)</b>: 0 rows.</p></div><p><b>Environment: dev</b> — dev deployment, build <code>8b4be94</code> (Deploy Convex, 2026-10-19T17:04:37Z); account and address are not written into the report; run folder <code>runs/2026-10-14-dev</code>, lane newspec-c (<code>newspec-c/results.json</code>, screenshots not attached).</p><p><b>Test method:</b> AICHECK · AI output check — as the lane wrote it; Source: <code>dev/newspec-c</code>.</p><p><b>UAT item:</b> TC-14 In-Room Dictation &amp; Note Generation · <b>Section:</b> A3 · Encounter · <b>Scenario:</b> TC-14/S46</p><p><b>TFA-95204 AC 3 / UAT 3.2: 5 Hospital + 5 Nursing Home hallucination-trap fixtures, a fixture passes only if no trap is invented in its note (9/10)</b></p><p><b>Tickets:</b> TFA-92592 In-Room Dictation &amp; Note Generation (ready for qa)</p><p><b>Lane in the dev run folder</b> <code>newspec-c</code>: status <b>failed</b> in <code>newspec-c/results.json</code> → <b>failed</b> (failed (the lane flagged no product issue)).</p><p><b>Detail:</b></p><pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">Dev <dev address> (main 8b4be94a), live models (every call Haiku 4.5 us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0, no fallback; generateNote providerMs 7.1–15.1 s, parsePreRoundNotes 4.5–5.3 s), under runs/.dev.lock, browsers in UTC; datasets hallu-hosp + hallu-nh (new specs hallu-hosp/-nh.spec.ts + hallu-lib.ts), 